---
title: MSIX Installer Execution from Malvertising or Fake Download Page
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f01
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of an MSIX installer shortly after a browser download event, matching FIN7's malvertising and fake software download page delivery vector (e.g. spoofed 7-Zip or browser update sites).
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.recordedfuture.com/research/grayalpha-uses-diverse-infection-vectors-deploy-powernet-loader-netsupport-rat
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1566
    - attack.execution
    - attack.t1204.002
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\AppInstaller.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: '.msix'
    parent_browser:
        ParentImage|endswith:
            - '\chrome.exe'
            - '\msedge.exe'
            - '\firefox.exe'
    condition: selection and parent_browser
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate MSIX-packaged software installed via approved enterprise channels
level: medium

---
title: BadUSB-Style Device Enumeration Followed by Rapid Process Execution
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f02
status: experimental
description: Detects a new HID/removable storage device enumeration immediately followed by process execution from a removable drive path, consistent with FIN7's mailed malicious USB delivery method.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/fin7
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1091
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|contains: ':\\'
        CommandLine|re: '^[D-Z]:\\\\.*\.exe'
    timeframe: 2m
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate use of approved USB drives for file transfer or provisioning
level: low

---
title: NetSupport RAT Process or Network Beacon on Unmanaged Endpoint
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f03
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of NetSupport Manager client binaries or associated network beaconing where the tool is not an approved remote-access solution, matching FIN7's repurposing of the commercial RAT as its primary payload.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/fin7-reboot-cybercrime-gang-enhances-ops-with-new-edr-bypasses-and-automated-attacks/
tags:
    - attack.command_and_control
    - attack.t1219
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_image:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\client32.exe'
            - '\remcmdstub.exe'
    selection_path_excl:
        Image|contains: '\Program Files\NetSupport\'
    condition: selection_image and not selection_path_excl
falsepositives:
    - IT help desk legitimately using NetSupport Manager from its approved install path
level: high

---
title: EDR/AV Service Tampering or Unexpected Termination
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f04
status: experimental
description: Detects endpoint security services being stopped, disabled, or crashing unexpectedly, consistent with FIN7's AvNeutralizer (AuKill) EDR impairment tool.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/fin7-reboot-cybercrime-gang-enhances-ops-with-new-edr-bypasses-and-automated-attacks/
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1562.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_sc:
        Image|endswith: '\sc.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'stop'
            - 'config'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'sc'
    selection_service_names:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'WinDefend'
            - 'SepMasterService'
            - 'Sense'
            - 'CSFalconService'
            - 'elastic-endpoint'
    condition: selection_sc and selection_service_names
falsepositives:
    - Authorized administrator performing planned EDR migration or maintenance
level: high

