---
title: Anubis Backdoor In-Memory Python Execution with Base64 C2
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f06
status: experimental
description: Detects a Python interpreter executing in-memory code with Base64-encoded command line content, consistent with reported behavior of the FIN7 Anubis backdoor.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://thehackernews.com/2025/06/anubis-ransomware-encrypts-and-wipes.html
tags:
    - attack.command_and_control
    - attack.t1071
    - attack.execution
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_python:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\python.exe'
            - '\pythonw.exe'
    selection_encoded:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '-c'
            - 'base64'
            - 'b64decode'
    condition: selection_python and selection_encoded
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate internal Python tooling using Base64 encoding for unrelated purposes
level: medium

---
title: Ransomware Encryptor with Destructive Wipe Behavior
id: 2d4e5f6a-7b8c-4d1e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f07
status: experimental
description: Detects mass file rename/overwrite activity combined with volume shadow copy deletion, consistent with FIN7-affiliated ransomware strains (e.g. Anubis) that include a destructive wipe mode.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://thehackernews.com/2025/06/anubis-ransomware-encrypts-and-wipes.html
tags:
    - attack.impact
    - attack.t1486
    - attack.t1490
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_vss:
        Image|endswith: '\vssadmin.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'delete shadows'
    selection_wmic:
        Image|endswith: '\wmic.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'shadowcopy delete'
    condition: selection_vss or selection_wmic
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate backup software or admin-initiated shadow copy cleanup
level: high

